  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its design, bulk, mass, scale and siting, would appear incongruous and out of keeping with the prevailing character of the host dwelling, the terrace row and the distinctiveness and historic character of the Becontree Estate. The proposal would overly dominate the rear of the host dwelling. It would present unsympathetic design with regard to the flat roof form, and result in a loss of symmetry across the terrace row. It would thereby cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the area, including&nbsp;moderate&nbsp;harm to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
